        "subject": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for remote MDT allocation",
        "message": "DRAFT LU-21180 lod: add kunit test for remote MDT allocation\n\nlod_mdt_alloc_rr() and lod_mdt_alloc_qos() pick remote MDTs for a\nstriped directory by calling dt_fid_alloc()/dt_locate_at() directly,\nwith no stubbable wrapper, so they had no kunit coverage: every other\nLOD allocator mock stubs that lookup instead of resolving it.\n\nAdd lod_mdt_alloc_test, covering round-robin and QoS-weighted\nselection, exhausted/degraded/too-few-MDTs paths, and OSS/MDS-spread\navoidance, by giving mock_tgt real object location/allocation\nsupport: mock_tgt_site_init() builds a tiny but real lu_site/\nlu_device/lu_object stack so dt_fid_alloc()+dt_locate_at() on a\nmock_tgt resolve to a real (if featureless) dt_object, instead of\nneeding a real OSD/OSP underneath.\n\nFix two mock_tgt bugs this test exposed, both pre-existing in the\nobject location/allocation support added for lod_tgt_test and\nlod_init_obj_test: every mock_tgt's dt_device needs a non-NULL\nld_type, because lu_object_put() dereferences it unconditionally;\nand mock_tgt_top_object_free() must call lu_object_fini() to drop\nthe top object's reference on the shared fake top device, or that\ndevice's ld_ref never returns to zero. Add mock_tgt_site_drain(),\nalso called from mock_tgt_site_fini(), to flush the site's delayed-\nfree list: dt_locate_at() hands out FID_SEQ_NORMAL-range objects,\nwhose last put lands them there rather than on the LRU that\nlu_site_purge() reclaims, so a test case must drain it before\nreusing or re-initializing the mock_tgt structs those objects are\nlayered on.\n\nExport lod_mdt_alloc_rr() and lod_mdt_alloc_qos() for the test\nmodule to call directly.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Ronnie Sahlberg <rsahlberg@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: AGENT:claude-sonnet-5 [claude-code]\nChange-Id: I9d1a0fbed6f1769203a8459ea293028096c476da\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
